124.m:
I cannot bear life, fortune, or high station;
I am wasted away seeing the sons born of Aditi.
I fall into an intolerable state, distressed,
beholding Aditi's supreme prosperity.
Even entering a forest fire surely brings happiness;
not even in a dream should a rival's splendor be witnessed.

Śambhu said:
"O sage, do not harbor anger against the husband of Śacī;
attain peace, O very wise one, for the Maruts have become immortals."

For all beings desiring fruits in this world and the next,
the attainment of a virtuous son is always cherished;
therefore, grant your favor with respect to bathing here."

Brahmā said:
From that time on, that holy place was called Putratīrtha;
there, through bathing, giving, and the like, one obtains all desires.

125.m:
The female owl said:
Terrified of you, people run after [dharma];
terrified of you, they practice celibacy;
terrified of you, the resolute act virtuously;
terrified of you, they become devoted to ritual acts.

Terrified of you, they undertake fasting to death;
terrified of you, they wander from the village to the forest;
terrified of you, they adopt gentleness;
terrified of you, they partake of soma-drinking;
terrified of you, they devote themselves to gifts of food and cattle;
terrified of you, they proclaim discourse on Brahman.

Brahmā said:
Both gods spoke to the two birds renowned in the world,
for the attainment of dharma and fame, desiring the welfare of the worlds:

fortunate, intelligent, heroic, and causing sons and grandsons to flourish.
By the offering of rice-balls and the like there, the ancestors attain release;
from sin born of mind, speech, and body, a person becomes freed by bathing.

128.m:
Śambhu said:
“From my seed and through you, Suvarṇa of immense power was born.
All prosperities completely abide in this Suvarṇa;
